  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Cyproterone (often as cyproterone acetate) is a steroidal antiandrogen used for conditions involving excess androgen effects, such as prostate cancer and androgen-related disorders. It is an approved medicine and remains in use, available in combination with estrogens as well as on its own.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7381206\">Wikidata Q7381206</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>cyproterone</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>G03HA01</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB04839\">DB04839</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/9880\">9880</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:50743\">50743</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7381206\">Q7381206</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C24H29ClO4</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>416.942 g/mol (PubChem CID 9880)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>3.1 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table><p><small>Drugs.Common 25.09 gave 374.9 g/mol (-10.1 %); replaced by the value above</small></p></body></html>"));
